    {
      "type": "discussion",
      "content": "(We stress that $ \\sigma_A^2 $ is the additive genetic variance accounted for by the QTL, not the trait as a whole.) A value of $ T $ significantly greater than $ N $ suggests linkage to a QTL. If the sample size within each marker class is sufficiently large, so that the observed value of $ SE^2 $ can be taken to be very close to the population value of $ \\sigma^2 $(MC), then the distribution of $ T $ is approximately $ \\chi^2 $ with $ N $ degrees of freedom.",
      "source_page": 512,
      "printed_page": 492,
      "source_block_ids": [
