    {
      "type": "discussion",
      "content": "A closely related, and more widely used, approach is a nested ANOVA (Neimann-Sørensen and Robertson 1961, Lowry and Schultz 1959), which considers marker effects nested within each sibship. We only briefly consider the properties of nested ANOVA here, as these are extensively discussed in Chapter 18 (where effects of dams are nested within those for sires for the different purpose of estimating genetic variance components summed over all loci). The basic linear model is",
      "source_page": 512,
      "printed_page": 492,
